# rc's cases for usbzig.rc: each "#### name" line starts a script that
# usbzig.rc runs with planZ's rc and with stock rc, in an empty
# directory of its own, with its own environment and standard input
# from /dev/null.  The environment starts empty but for true and false,
# which 9front has as no programs:
#	fn true { status='' }
#	fn false { status=false }
# $RC is the rc under test, for the scripts' own child shells; a plain
# "rc" is always the stock one.  The two outputs, with errors and the
# final status, must be the same once pids, addresses and the path of
# planZ's rc are masked.  An error ends a script, as in any rc, so the
# fatal ones run in a child, $RC -c.
